---
description: Read the current :DatasetTransform joins[] for an output dataset
argument-hint: <output_dataset_uri>
---

Read the current dataset-shape state for `$ARGUMENTS` (an `output_dataset_uri` of the form `dprod:ds:{contract_id}:{schema_physical_name}`).

```bash
curl -s "{{ backend_base_url }}/api/projects/{{ project.id }}/dataset-transform?output_dataset_uri=$ARGUMENTS"
```

The response includes `joins`, `filter`, `dedupe`, `grouping_keys`, `scd_policy`, `suppressed_columns`, `grain_prose`. Engineer overrides only touch `joins[]` — the others are PO-authored in the wizard.

Empty `joins` means FK auto-discovery is in charge. A non-empty list means an explicit join graph is being used (and FK auto-discovery is bypassed entirely).
